Spec: TenantInstallScript

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  Orchestrate the install of one `TenantInstance`: run the package's category buckets in a fixed
    order through `@import_run` — `install_pre` hook, `befores`, `vitals`, tofu, first-run
    `init_from`, `others`, `scalables`, `posts` — then pick between backup scheduling and backup
    cleanup, run `install_post`, and close by writing the CR `Ready`/`Installed` status with the
    requested tag. This file applies no manifests and waits on nothing itself: per-lane cluster
    work and per-lane failure markers live in the stage modules it imports; its own only status
    write is the success close. There is no `crds` lane: the tenant CRD family carries no
    CRD-stage surface at all (no `CrdApplied` condition, no crd bridge — /common/src/instancetenant.sdd).
  Twin: near-clone of ./../service/install.rhai — an actual `diff -u` shows exactly two hunks: the
    tenant copy drops the whole taken-`crds` block (the `is_dir` gate, its `@log_info` line,
    `@import_run("install_crds")`, the @update_k8s_crd_cache call and its refresh) and renames
    every instance refresh from @get_service_instance to @get_tenant_instance (six sites instead
    of seven). Hook posture, the five remaining `is_dir` gates, the tofu lane merge posture, the
    `init_from` and backup gate texts, the `backup-settings` Secret probe with its @try/@catch,
    and the status close are byte-identical. Tenant-only surface (the `context.tenant`
    maintenance window fields, tenant-wide namespaces and services) is assembled upstream in
    ./context_tenant.rhai and read nowhere here; the tenant backup flow this lane schedules stays
    behind ./schedule_backup.rhai, which applies backup objects over `context.tenant.namespaces`
    and records failures under the `ScheduleBackup` condition. ./../system/install.rhai is the
    different shape (single `systems` bucket, no vitals, no `init_from`, no backup section).

Exposes:
  @run(@instance, @context) — the module's sole @fn and entry point (`install.rhai` + `run` match
    the entry-point patterns of /agent/src/linting/rhai_checker.sdd); invoked as
    `install::run(instance, context)` by the Rust lane /agent/src/tenant/install.sdd, whose
    snippet discards the returned value.

Accepts:
  @instance — the injected @TenantInstance @Dynamic. Read: `.metadata.namespace`/`.metadata.name`
    (every refresh argument), the guards `.status != ()`, `.status.vitals != ()`, @type_of of
    `.status.tag`, and `.spec.initFrom` (the @InitFrom restore source, wire key `initFrom`).
    Re-bound after most taken buckets (Must).
  @context — map built by ./context.rhai @run for this lane: ./../lib/build_context.rhai core
    keys merged with the tenant additions of ./context_tenant.rhai. Keys read, all unguarded
    property access: `package_dir` (six gate paths), `namespace.use_backup` (backup gate; the
    `context.namespace` map is the `context.tenant` map aliased by ./context_tenant.rhai, seeded
    `false`, overridable only by a `vynil.solidite.fr/use_backup` namespace annotation decoding
    to a bool), `instance.requested` (the tag of the final close) and `instance.namespace` (the
    backup-Secret lookup namespace — the tenant instance's own namespace, not the tenant-wide
    list).

Returns:
  No value channel of its own: the function's implicit value is the trailing
    `@set_status_ready` call result (the patched CR) and the caller discards it. The observable
    outcome is the final `status` patch on the TenantInstance — the children-variant close evicts
    prior `AgentStarted`, `BeforeApplied`, `Ready`, `Installed`, `InitFrom` and `ScheduleBackup`
    records and appends fresh `Ready`/`Installed` at the current generation, sets `tag` to
    `instance.requested` and `digest` to the options digest, and publishes a Normal
    `InstallSucceed`/`Install` event (bridge and macro semantics in
    /common/src/instancetenant.sdd and /common/src/instance_macros.sdd).

Raises:
  Zero @throw statement in this file: failure is always a propagated engine raise.
  - Stage/hook module throw: @import_run swallows only the absent-module and absent-`run`
    markers (`log_debug` with text `No ${name} module, skipping.` /
    `No ${name}::run function, skipping.`); any other error — including everything a stage
    re-throws after writing its own marker (e.g. @set_status_init_failed,
    @set_status_schedule_backup_failed) — is re-thrown and aborts the install.
  - `@get_tenant_instance` raise (CR deleted, forbidden or unreachable) at a bucket refresh —
    the abort lands with no failed-status write from this lane.
  - @has_tofu_files raise: the gate runs on an unreadable existing `${package_dir}/tofu` past its
    `@is_dir` guard (raise rules in ./../lib/tofu_gen.sdd).
  - Property-on-`()` raises at the `context.namespace.use_backup` /
    `context.instance.requested` reads once `context` stops being a map (see Tasks — the tofu
    lane can set it to `()`).
  - `@set_status_ready` raise: a @KubeError from the merge-patch/event, or a non-string
    `instance.requested`, fails an otherwise-complete install with no marker written.
  - The one @try/@catch: the `backup-settings` Secret probe — every error from its @get is
    caught (string warned verbatim, other errors as @json_encode text) and treated as "absent",
    never re-thrown.

Handles:
  - Bucket-directory absent: the `@is_dir` gate (`@has_tofu_files` for tofu) skips the whole lane
    including its instance refresh — skipped buckets never call `@get_tenant_instance`.
  - `install_pre` / `install_post` ship nowhere under ./../scripts — on a stock image both hooks
    take the @import_run skip path, return `()`, and the `type_of` merge guard sees no map.
  - Package carrying a `crds/` directory: ignored entirely by this lane — there is no crd bucket
    or crd bridge on the tenant kind (see Purpose); package CRD management needs another actor.
  - First run: `status` is `()` at entry, so the `init_from` gate is false until the `vitals`
    bucket has written `status.vitals` and the refresh re-read it — that is the exact
    "initial installation" moment the code comment names.
  - Backup gate false (no status, no vitals, or `use_backup` false — the shipped default from
    ./context_tenant.rhai): still runs `delete_backup` — every stock tenant install sweeps
    stale backup objects.
  - Backup-Secret probe error: warned, `found` stays false, the lane degrades to
    `delete_backup` — a permission or transient API error reads as "no backup configured"
    (see Tasks).

Must:
  Run exactly these lanes, once each, in this order: `import_run("install_pre")`;
    `is_dir(`${context.package_dir}/befores`)` gate → `install_befores`; `vitals` gate →
    `install_vitals`; `tfg::has_tofu_files(`${context.package_dir}/tofu`)` gate →
    `install_tofu`;
    `instance.status != () && instance.status.vitals != () && type_of(instance.status.tag) == "()"
    && instance.spec.initFrom != ()` gate → `init_from`; `others` gate → `install_others`;
    `scalables` gate → `install_scalables`; `posts` gate → `install_posts`; backup section;
    `import_run("install_post")`; `instance.set_status_ready(context.instance.requested)` —
    then return, with nothing after the close.
  Gate the first install exactly as written: `init_from` runs only when the CR already reports
    `status.vitals`, its `status.tag` is still unset (`type_of` == `"()"`) and `spec.initFrom` is
    set — so a completed install (tag written by the close) never runs it again even though the
    tenant spec's `initFrom` stays set.
  Decide backups on `instance.status != () && instance.status.vitals != () &&
    context.namespace.use_backup`: when true, schedule only if
    `@k8s_resource("Secret", context.instance.namespace).@get("backup-settings")` succeeds —
    `schedule_backup` — and `delete_backup` on probe-absent-or-any-error; when false,
    unconditionally `delete_backup`. Exactly one of the two runs per install, and the code
    comment pins `schedule_backup` behind the `scalables` lane ("this need the scalables objects
    to be set").
  Thread the context through a map merge only on `@type_of` == `map` of each hook/bucket return —
    `install_pre`, the five `is_dir` buckets and `install_post` use the guard; the `install_tofu`
    lane instead assigns the return unconditionally and then re-applies the stale `ctx` variable
    when that is a map (Tasks); `init_from`, `schedule_backup` and `delete_backup` have their
    returns discarded whole.
  Refresh the instance after each taken bucket with
    `@get_tenant_instance(instance.metadata.namespace, instance.metadata.name)` — the tenant
    bridge registered onto @TenantInstance::rhai_get (six call sites; service's seventh crds
    refresh has no counterpart). The refreshed copy is what the `init_from`/backup guards and the
    close read; the `init_from` and backup lanes themselves never refresh.
  Keep the two @log_warn calls inside the probe catch the only log statements at this level —
    unlike the service twin, this file issues no @log_info (its crds-lane log line does not
    exist here); `install_pre`-style debug text comes from the @import_run shim only.
  Close successfully through @set_status_ready with the requested tag (build_context's
    `instance.requested` = `args.tag`), which also stamps the options digest and can fail the
    whole install per Raises.
  Load ./../lib/tofu_gen.rhai (and transitively ./../lib/tofu.rhai) at import time via the single
    top-level `import "tofu_gen" as tfg` — before any `run` call, package without `.tf` files
    included.
  Resolve every stage/hook module against the four resolver directories frozen by the Rust lane
    (`{package_dir}/scripts`, `{config_dir}`, `{script_dir}/tenant`, `{script_dir}/lib`), so a
    package `scripts/` directory shadows the shipped lanes: a package shadowing `install_tofu`
    must return the context map or `context` becomes `()` mid-run (Tasks).

Must not:
  Apply manifests, render templates or wait on workloads from this file: apply ordering lives in
    ./../lib/install_from_dir.sdd and readiness in ./../lib/wait.sdd, both reached only through
    the stage modules — importing either here would duplicate the lane contract.
  Read or honor the tenant maintenance window (`context.tenant.maintenance_start_hour`/
    `maintenance_start_minut`, `maintenance_start`/`maintenance_stop` modules): maintenance
    belongs to the backup/restore lanes; the install closes without any maintenance signal.
  Gate on the current `status.tag` to skip a rerun: replays are total; only the `init_from` and
    backup guards read prior status.

Depends on:
  ./../lib/tofu_gen.rhai — the only import; @has_tofu_files answers the `tofu` gate (its spec
    ./../lib/tofu_gen.sdd).
  The shipped stage modules of this directory, all specs pending: ./install_befores.rhai,
    ./install_vitals.rhai, ./install_tofu.rhai, ./init_from.rhai, ./install_others.rhai,
    ./install_scalables.rhai, ./install_posts.rhai, ./schedule_backup.rhai,
    ./delete_backup.rhai — each writes its own `set_status_*` / `set_status_*_failed` marker and
    re-throws, and each returns the (maybe hook-merged) context. Tenant stage markers include the
    tenant-carried `InitFrom` and `ScheduleBackup` stages.
  vynil-core 0.7.7 engine API — the three-arg @import_run global shim injected by @Script
    `add_common` (optional-import semantics, skip-vs-rethrow boundary quoted in Raises), @is_dir,
    @log_debug/@log_warn, @json_encode and @k8s_resource(...).@get.
  /common/src/instancetenant.sdd — the registered bridges used as methods/globals:
    @get_tenant_instance → @TenantInstance::rhai_get and @set_status_ready →
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_ready; close and event semantics in
    /common/src/instance_macros.sdd.
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — the @Script constructor that mounts the above for the agent
    lanes.
  ./context.rhai (+ ./context_tenant.rhai, ./../lib/build_context.rhai) — producer of every
    `context` key this file reads; shared keys owned by ./../lib/build_context.sdd, the tenant
    `namespace`/`use_backup` aliasing by ./context_tenant.rhai's pending spec.

References:
  /agent/src/tenant/install.sdd — the caller: snippet, `instance`/`args` injection, resolver
    directories and the exit-1 error lane this script's raises land in.
  ./../service/install.rhai and ./../service/install.sdd — the diff-verified twin this spec
    calibrates against; the tenant copy shares the tofu-lane merge posture verbatim.
  ./../system/install.rhai — the different-shaped third lane (unspecified yet).
  /agent/tests/rhai_backup_redis.rs — the tenant mock-engine harness (lib + tenant resolver dirs,
    mock `"TenantInstance"` values) — proof the tenant scripts test under mocks, but it imports
    only the backup-prepare/restore modules, never `install` (Tasks).
  /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs — mounts the service dirs only and never loads a tenant script;
    no test runs this file (Tasks).

Scenario: full bucket order with directories present
  Given a tenant package dir holding all six category directories and tofu sources, on a live
    engine
  When @run executes
  Then the stage modules are imported in exactly pre → befores → vitals → tofu → others →
    scalables → posts → backup → post order, with @get_tenant_instance refreshing after each
    taken bucket and no CRD apply or discovery-cache refresh anywhere
  And the close runs last whatever the buckets returned
  No mapped test: the harnesses never import the tenant `install` module.

Scenario: absent modules and empty package skip clean
  Given a stock image (no `install_pre`/`install_post` ship) on a package with no category dirs
  When @run executes
  Then both hooks, the five buckets, tofu and init_from skip silently (debug logs only), the
    backup section still runs `delete_backup`, and @set_status_ready is reached
  No mapped test; the service twin's @service_install_runs_without_error posture (catch-and-assert
    any error) would at most prove reachability here if mirrored (Tasks).

Scenario: init_from fires only during the very first install
  Given a TenantInstance with `spec.initFrom` set whose `status.vitals` was just written by the
    vitals bucket and whose `status.tag` is unset
  When the `init_from` gate is evaluated over the refreshed instance
  Then @import_run("init_from") runs — its return and any hook-merged context are discarded
  But given the same CR after a successful close wrote `status.tag`
  Then the gate is false and `init_from` never runs again, and that later close evicts any
    stale `InitFrom` and `ScheduleBackup` condition records
  No mapped test.

Scenario: backup branch table
  Given vitals applied and `context.namespace.use_backup` true (namespace annotation override)
    and the `backup-settings` Secret readable in `context.instance.namespace`
    → @schedule_backup runs, @delete_backup does not
  Given the same with the Secret missing OR its read erroring (warned) → @delete_backup runs
  Given `use_backup` false (shipped default) or no `status.vitals` → @delete_backup runs
  And in every branch the module's return is discarded and the flow continues to `install_post`
  No mapped test.

Scenario: stage throw aborts after its own marker
  Given a bucket stage that fails — it writes its `set_status_*_failed` marker (e.g.
    @set_status_init_failed, @set_status_schedule_backup_failed) and re-throws
  When the throw crosses @import_run
  Then it is not one of the two skip markers, so it re-throws: no later bucket, no close, and
    the Rust lane fails to exit(1) — a failure raised inside THIS file instead (refresh,
    tofu predicate, close) leaves no failed-marker at all
  No mapped test.

Scenario: tofu context merge clobber
  Given the befores/vitals lanes returned maps (the shipped stages always do) and a tofu gate
    that is true
  When @run reaches the tofu exit
  Then `context` first becomes install_tofu's return and is then OVERWRITTEN by the stale `ctx`
    still holding the pre-tofu merge — tofu-lane context updates (e.g. `context.tofu`) reach
    `install_post` and the close only when no earlier lane merged
  No mapped test; recorded behavior, see Tasks (shared verbatim with the service twin).

Tasks:
  [ ] Map the Scenarios with a tenant install suite: /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs is
      service-only and never loads the tenant dir; /agent/tests/rhai_backup_redis.rs shows the
      tenant mock harness works but only for the backup-prepare/restore modules. Add a fixture
      package with the six category dirs and mocks for the refs, pinning order/refresh/gates.
  [?] Tofu-lane double assignment: `context = import_run("install_tofu", ...)` plus the stale
      `ctx` re-merge (Scenario "tofu context merge clobber") drops install_tofu's context on
      every package that has an earlier merged lane. Decide once for both twins — the tenant
      copy shares the service shape byte-for-byte.
  [?] `init_from`, `schedule_backup` and `delete_backup` returns are discarded while every
      other hook result is merged — decide whether their `*_pre`/`*_post` hook context updates
      are meant to propagate downstream (today: they do not).
  [?] The backup-Secret probe funnels EVERY read error (Forbidden included) into "absent" →
      `delete_backup`, which sweeps the tenant's backup objects — a transient or rbac error can
      therefore drop a tenant backup schedule. Decide whether to narrow to NotFound (twin-shared
      with /agent/scripts/service/install.sdd).
  [?] `install_pre`/`install_post` ship in no engine directory, so they exist only as
      package-side hooks ({package_dir}/scripts). Confirm that is intentional (twin-shared).
  [?] A package shadowing `install_tofu` with a module whose `run` returns non-map leaves
      `context` = `()` and the install dies on the next property read (here:
      `context.namespace.use_backup`). Decide whether to guard with the `type_of` pattern or
      make it a documented package-author contract a linter should catch (twin-shared).
  [?] Tenant-only: the context carries the maintenance window (`maintenance_start_hour`/
      `maintenance_start_minut`) yet the tenant install ignores it entirely — first install of a
      maintenance-sensitive tenant applies vitals/scalables at any hour. Confirm only
      backup/restore are maintenance-gated by design.
  [?] Twin-drift watch: this file is currently the service twin minus the crds lane plus the
      refresh rename; `update_k8s_crd_cache` is imported by neither kind's tenant-side module,
      so a future service fix must be hand-copied here. Decide whether the orchestrator body
      should be factored into a shared lib module with a kind hook.

Done when:
  Every Scenario carries a passing mapped test or a recorded decision, the bucket/hook order and
    gate texts above still match the source, and `specdd lint` is green on this file.
